# PowerShell scripts are executed on a Windows guest: keep CRLF in the working tree so the file the
# guest runs looks native, and keep them TEXT so they are diffable. The load-bearing property is that
# these files stay ASCII-ONLY (see WINDOWS_TOOLCHAIN.md): PowerShell 5.1 reads a BOM-less file as ANSI,
# so a UTF-8 em-dash decodes to bytes containing a double quote, which desyncs string parsing and yields
# phantom "Missing closing '}'" errors. Line endings alone are not the hazard; encoding is.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
